A stronger result emerged from replay: the exact rung-34 slice point automatically satisfies every restored and late graph row through rung 38 (164/164), without solving rungs 36 or 38 separately. Only nine band-40 rows remain nonzero at that point; the current continuation slice targets precisely that first residual block.
